  "note": "Polled Wednesday 18 May 1955 and counted on Thursday 19 May by W. G. Best, returning officer. Thirteen candidates for twelve seats: \"All 12 Unionists elected\"; the one Independent, Dr Donnell Deeny, was defeated. 7,447 qualified to vote and 4,953 voted (66.51 per cent); 20 papers spoilt."
